 "11.7:code": "BOTTOM LINE\nThe pilot cut median claim handling time by 27% (very likely between 24% and 30%) across 1,140 claims.\nRolled out to all motor adjusters, that frees about 16,007 adjuster hours a year. Recommend rollout in Q1.\nDecision needed by 15 November: rollout budget ($380,000) and two weeks of IT time for SSO and the policy API.\n\nECONOMICS (annual, at 85% adoption)\n  value of time freed     $992,464\n  run cost                $38,556  ($0.42 per claim)\n  net                     $953,908   conservative case: $847,612\n  payback                 4.8 months   conservative case: 5.4 months\n\nHOW WE MEASURED\n  620 claims without and 1,140 with the assistant, same team, 6 weeks; medians to limit outlier effects.\n\nRISKS\n  - Gains may shrink on complex claims (pilot skewed to standard motor claims) -> track by claim type in rollout.\n  - Adoption below 85% lowers value proportionally -> training and in-tool feedback.\n\nASKS\n  - Budget approval (CFO) by 15 Nov  - IT: Entra ID app registration and policy API access by 22 Nov",
 "11.7:lab": "Status AMBER: SSO app registration blocked 5 days; answer quality below target. Pilot start at risk by 4 days unless SSO lands this week.\nHeadline: adjusters now get a correct, sourced answer for 8 in 10 questions (was 7 last week; target 9).\nThat avoids about 176 escalations a month at current volume.\nDone: 300-claim test set built with the claims team.\nNext: review screen in the pilot (review UI in pilot); closing the quality gap to 9 in 10.\nIncident: index was out of date for 6 hours on Tuesday; fixed, and an alert now catches it.\nAsk: IT (M. Rossi) to complete SSO app registration by Fri 30 Oct.\n\nlines: 7 | model jargon present: []",
 "11.8:code": "10 notes -> 4 themes\n\n1. [sync permission sharepoint] score 17.9 | 3 customers, $2.7M ARR, 46 FDE days lost\n   e.g. \"Need group-level permission sync for SharePoint, page-level sync is too slow\" (initech)\n2. [eval trace case] score 10.3 | 3 customers, $2.5M ARR, 9 FDE days lost\n   e.g. \"Eval sets: no way to turn traces into eval cases without export\" (hooli)\n3. [private batch api] score 8.9 | 2 customers, $2.1M ARR, 14 FDE days lost\n   e.g. \"Private networking for the batch API in EU regions is missing\" (stark)\n4. [dark mode admin] score 3.1 | 1 customer, $0.9M ARR, 1 FDE days lost\n   e.g. \"Dark mode for the admin console\" (globex)",
