 "12.4:code": "plan: 4 sub-questions | searches used: 5 | sources: ['s1', 's2', 's3', 's4', 's5']\nREPORT\n  - Only 12% of surveyed enterprises run autonomous agents in production. [s3, 2026-05]\n  - In a 2026 survey of 1,200 firms, 64% had at least one generative AI application in production. [s1, 2026-03]\n  - Average generative AI budgets grew 38% year over year according to the vendor's customer base. [s2, 2025-11]\n  - The EU AI Act's obligations for general-purpose AI models have applied since August 2025. [s5, 2026-04]\nremoved by citation check: [('Half of enterprises run autonomous agents in production', 's3')]\nskipped as outdated or duplicate: s4 (2024), s6 (syndicated copy of s1)",
 "12.4:lab": "rule         searches  coverage  important  searches per source\nfixed20          20.0     73.6%      50.1%                 0.68\ntwo_dry          15.5     65.5%      41.0%                 0.59\ngood_turing      14.8     63.8%      38.7%                 0.58\n\nGood-Turing stopping saves 26% of searches for 10 points less coverage,\nbut loses 11 points on the rare, important sources: more of the same query mostly re-finds popular pages.\nRecommendation: stop early on diminishing returns, and spend the saved budget on diversified queries\n(different phrasings, primary-source sites, other languages), which is what reaches the rare sources.",
