 "12.6:lab": "router           hit rate  TTFT mean  TTFT p99  max/mean load\nround_robin         69.6%       562ms      800ms           1.00\nleast_loaded        69.6%       563ms      808ms           1.02\nprefix_hash_bounded    99.3%       489ms      556ms           1.24\n\nBounded load stops the most popular prefixes from overloading one replica: overflow spills to the next replica on the ring,\nwhich then also caches that prefix, so hot prefixes end up replicated on a few replicas instead of one.",
 "13.1:code": "one-off cost of fine-tuning: $27,500  (labelling (4,000 examples reviewed), training runs and evals, engineering (2 weeks))\nper request: large prompted $9.60/1k, fine-tuned small $0.50/1k\n   50,000 req/month: large $      480  small $   1,025  saving $     -545  payback   inf months -> stay prompted\n  300,000 req/month: large $    2,880  small $   1,149  saving $    1,731  payback  15.9 months -> stay prompted\n1,000,000 req/month: large $    9,600  small $   1,498  saving $    8,102  payback   3.4 months -> fine-tune (if evals match)\n5,000,000 req/month: large $   48,000  small $   3,490  saving $   44,510  payback   0.6 months -> fine-tune (if evals match)\nmonthly break-even (ignoring one-off): 109,866 requests; one-off adds the payback period above",
 "13.1:lab": "  total              3000\n  roles              0\n  bad_json           60\n  missing_fields     87\n  exact_duplicates   286\n  eval_leakage       16/300\n  pii_records        114\n  length_p50_p99     (98, 163)\n  clean_size         2567\n\ninvalid 4.9% | decision: NO-GO until fixed\nactions: drop invalid and duplicate records; remove 16 leaked eval items (or re-split by policy id); mask PII in 114 records; note that every 'vehicle' label is '?' (labels need review before training).",
 "13.2:code": "base model, source task accuracy: 1.000\nfew-shot (frozen, 20 examples)     target acc 0.656   trainable params      0\nnew head only (linear probe)       target acc 0.717   trainable params    260   base W changed: False\nLoRA r=4 + head                    target acc 0.776   trainable params   2116   base W changed: False\nfull fine-tune                     target acc 0.800   trainable params  25924   base W changed: True\n\nLoRA trains 8% of the parameters full fine-tuning trains, and the frozen base can serve other adapters.",
 "13.2:lab": "overall: large 0.883, LoRA 0.897, difference +0.013 (95% CI -0.003 to +0.030)\n  motor      n=306  large 0.899  LoRA 0.935  +0.036 \n  home       n=155  large 0.871  LoRA 0.903  +0.032 \n  travel     n= 78  large 0.859  LoRA 0.872  +0.013 \n  liability  n= 61  large 0.869  LoRA 0.721  -0.148 <- worse\ngeneral instructions: large 0.920, LoRA 0.870 (regression -0.050)\nmonthly cost: large $23,600 | LoRA $1,960 | routed $4,160 (routed accuracy 0.912)\n\nDECISION: ship with routing. The tuned model is at least as accurate overall and much cheaper, but worse on liability\nclaims and on general instructions. Route liability and any input the claim classifier cannot place to the large model;\nsend the rest to the LoRA model. Saves $19,440/month at equal or better accuracy. Collect more liability\nexamples for the next adapter version and re-run this comparison when either model changes.",
