 "14.2:lab": "8B fp16                KV   128 KiB/tok | fits   52 x 8k seqs | decode batch 1    203 tok/s | batch 52    3967 tok/s (  76/seq) | prefill 4k   132 ms\n70B fp16               weights   141 GB do not fit in 80 GB\nwhat-ifs:\n8B int8 weights        KV   128 KiB/tok | fits   59 x 8k seqs | decode batch 1    392 tok/s | batch 59    4982 tok/s (  84/seq) | prefill 4k   132 ms\n8B 32k context         KV   128 KiB/tok | fits   13 x 32k seqs | decode batch 1    185 tok/s | batch 13     992 tok/s (  76/seq) | prefill 4k   132 ms\n70B fp16, TP=4         KV   320 KiB/tok | fits   54 x 8k seqs | decode batch 1     80 tok/s | batch 54    2878 tok/s (  53/seq) | prefill 4k   344 ms\n70B int8, 1 GPU        weights fit (71 GB) but no room for even one 8k-token KV cache\n\nTalking points: decode is bandwidth bound, so batching multiplies throughput until KV memory runs out; int8 weights\nfree memory and halve weight reads; long contexts cut concurrency proportionally; TP=4 makes 70B fit with room for KV.",
